Subject: [PATCH] decoder: reject 'sato' items without input image items

validate_source_items() accepted a 'sato' derived image item with no 'dimg'
input image items ("between 0 and 32"). generate_tiles() creates no tiles for
the sato item itself, so every tile list stays empty, and create_codecs()
then indexed self.tiles[0][0] in can_use_single_codec() (decoder/mod.rs:1593,
index out of bounds) from next_image(). libavif rejects such a file at parse
time ("Box[sato] item %u has no input image items",
AVIF_RESULT_BMFF_PARSE_FAILED); do the same, like the empty-'iovl' check.
Not fixed upstream as of 5a494fc (2026-10-05).
Test: sato_without_input_items.

diff --git a/src/decoder/mod.rs b/src/decoder/mod.rs
index 888edc1..167743c 100644
--- a/src/decoder/mod.rs
+++ b/src/decoder/mod.rs
@@ -924,6 +924,10 @@ impl Decoder {
                 return AvifError::invalid_image_grid("invalid tmap items");
             }
         } else if item.is_sample_transform_item() {
+            // A 'sato' derived image item must reference at least one input image item.
+            if source_items.is_empty() {
+                return AvifError::bmff_parse_failed("no dimg items found for sato");
+            }
             if source_items.len() > 32 {
                 return AvifError::invalid_image_grid(
                     "expected sato to between 0 and 32 dimg items",
